---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";

const PUBLISHED = "2026-05-16";
const MODIFIED = "2026-05-16";
const URL = "https://tibiaplan.com/guides/tibia-stamina";

const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "Tibia Stamina Guide: Happy Hours, Regen, and the 14h Penalty",
  description:
    "How Tibia stamina actually works: the 3 XP zones, regen rates (3:1 vs 6:1), the +10 min initial delay, what doesn't drain stamina, the daily-reward online regen, and the Stamina Extension potion.",
  datePublished: PUBLISHED,
  dateModified: MODIFIED,
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "TibiaPlan" },
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: "TibiaPlan",
    url: "https://tibiaplan.com",
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": URL },
  url: URL,
};
---

<Layout
  title="Tibia Stamina Guide: Happy Hours, Regen & The 14h Penalty - TibiaPlan"
  description="The exact math of Tibia stamina: 3 XP zones, 3:1 vs 6:1 regen, the 10-min initial delay, what doesn't drain stamina, and how to refill online."
  keywords={[
    "tibia stamina",
    "tibia happy hours",
    "tibia stamina regen",
    "stamina extension potion",
    "tibia 42 hours",
  ]}
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-10">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_280px]">
      <article class="rounded-md border border-border-subtle bg-bg-surface p-6 sm:p-10">
        <header>
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-violet">
            Guide · Stamina
          </p>
          <h1 class="mt-2 text-[26px] font-medium leading-tight tracking-wide text-text-primary sm:text-[30px]">
            Tibia Stamina Guide: Happy Hours, Regen &amp; The 14h Penalty
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-text-tertiary">
            6 min read · Updated May 2026
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Tibia's stamina system is small in screen-space — just a number in
            the corner — but it controls how much experience and loot you get
            for every minute of hunting. The
            <a href="/" class="text-accent-violet hover:underline">Stamina mini-calc</a>
            on the home page tells you how long to wait offline. This guide
            explains what those numbers mean and where the misconceptions
            usually hide.
          </p>
        </header>

        <!-- Mobile TOC -->
        <nav class="mt-8 rounded-md border border-border-subtle bg-bg-sunken p-4 lg:hidden">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-text-tertiary">
            On this page
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-[12px] text-text-secondary">
            <li><a href="#basics" class="hover:text-accent-violet">1. The basics</a></li>
            <li><a href="#zones" class="hover:text-accent-violet">2. The three XP zones</a></li>
            <li><a href="#color-vs-effect" class="hover:text-accent-violet">3. Bar color vs actual effect</a></li>
            <li><a href="#drain" class="hover:text-accent-violet">4. What drains stamina (and what doesn't)</a></li>
            <li><a href="#regen-offline" class="hover:text-accent-violet">5. Offline regen — 3:1, 6:1, +10 min delay</a></li>
            <li><a href="#regen-online" class="hover:text-accent-violet">6. Online regen (Daily Reward)</a></li>
            <li><a href="#potion" class="hover:text-accent-violet">7. Stamina Extension potion</a></li>
            <li><a href="#playstyle" class="hover:text-accent-violet">8. Practical playstyle tips</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <!-- === Section 1: Basics === -->
        <section id="basics" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            1. The basics
          </h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <li>
              Full stamina is <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">42:00</span> (42 hours).
            </li>
            <li>
              Stamina <em class="not-italic font-semibold">only</em> drains when
              you actually gain experience from killing a monster. Idling,
              training, making runes, and getting hit by monsters
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">do not</span> drain
              it.
            </li>
            <li>
              The first kill from a no-combat state always drains a
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">minimum of 2 minutes</span> —
              this protects against re-logging tricks.
            </li>
            <li>
              Stamina only matters for premium accounts in one specific way
              (the Happy Hours bonus). The rest of the system applies to
              everyone.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 2: Three zones === -->
        <section id="zones" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            2. The three XP zones
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Stamina's only job is to scale your XP per kill. There are three
            distinct rates depending on how much stamina you have left:
          </p>

          <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[12px]">
              <thead class="border-b border-border-subtle text-text-tertiary">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Zone</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Stamina range</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">XP multiplier</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Notes</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-text-secondary">
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2"><span class="font-semibold text-success">Happy Hours</span></td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">39:00 – 42:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-success">150%</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">+50% bonus — <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">premium only</span>. Free accounts get 100% in this range.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2"><span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Normal</span></td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">14:00 – 39:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right">100%</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">Where you spend most of your hunting time.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2"><span class="font-semibold text-danger">Penalty</span></td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">0:01 – 14:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-danger">50%</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">Plus: monsters drop <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">no loot</span> if you dealt the most damage, and no coop loot at all.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2"><span class="font-semibold text-danger">Empty</span></td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">0:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-danger">0%</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">No XP and no loot at all. Log out and refill.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">A note on free vs premium:</span>
            the +50% Happy Hours bonus is the only XP modifier locked behind
            premium. The normal-zone 100% rate and the below-14h penalty
            apply equally to everyone.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 3: Color vs effect === -->
        <section id="color-vs-effect" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            3. Bar color vs actual effect
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            This is where most players get confused. The in-game stamina bar
            uses
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">two colors</span>:
          </p>

          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-success">Green</span> — when
              you're in the Happy Hours range (39:00 – 42:00).
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-danger">Red</span> — anywhere
              below 39:00, all the way down to 0:00.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            But the
            <em class="not-italic font-semibold">XP penalty</em>
            only kicks in below 14:00. So the bar can look red and feel like
            a warning, but if you're at, say, 25:00, you're still earning
            100% XP — just no bonus. The red color from 14:00 to 39:00 is
            "you're out of bonus", not "you're being penalised".
          </p>

          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Rule of thumb:</span>
            trust the
            <em class="not-italic">number</em>, not the colour. As long as
            your stamina reads 14:00 or higher, your XP is at 100% (or 150%
            if you're a premium in the green range).
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 4: Drain === -->
        <section id="drain" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            4. What drains stamina (and what doesn't)
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Stamina drains at
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">exactly 1:1</span>
            with real-world time — every minute you spend gaining XP from a
            monster kill drains 1 minute of stamina. The zone you're in
            (green / red / penalty) doesn't change the drain rate; only the
            XP multiplier.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 text-[14px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            What does NOT drain stamina
          </h3>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <li>Training on dummies (regular or exercise weapons).</li>
            <li>Being attacked by monsters without killing any.</li>
            <li>Killing summoned monsters (your own or a teammate's).</li>
            <li>Making runes, casting spells, mana-sitting.</li>
            <li>Travel, depot management, chat, quests with no kills.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="mt-5 text-[14px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            The 2-minute minimum drain
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            When you initiate combat after being out of combat, the
            <em class="not-italic">first</em> kill drains a minimum of
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">2 minutes</span> of
            stamina, even if the fight took 5 seconds. This stops players
            from re-logging to dodge stamina drain on quick kills.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 5: Offline regen === -->
        <section id="regen-offline" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            5. Offline regen — 3:1, 6:1, and the 10-minute delay
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            The default way to refill stamina is to log out. Two rules
            govern the regen rate:
          </p>

          <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[12px]">
              <thead class="border-b border-border-subtle text-text-tertiary">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Stamina range being refilled</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Regen ratio</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Meaning</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-text-secondary">
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">Below 39:00 (red zone)</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">3 : 1</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">3 minutes offline = 1 minute of stamina back</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">39:00 – 42:00 (green / bonus)</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono font-semibold text-accent-cyan">6 : 1</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">6 minutes offline = 1 minute of stamina back (twice as slow)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="mt-5 text-[14px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            The +10 minute initial delay
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Stamina does
            <em class="not-italic font-semibold">not</em> start regenerating
            the moment you log out. The character needs to be logged off for
            a continuous
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">10 minutes</span>
            before any regen begins. This is the same 10 minutes whether
            you're at 41:00 or at 0:00 — it's a fixed start-up cost.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Short hunting breaks lose disproportionately to this delay.
            Logging off for 8 minutes and back in gets you
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">zero</span>
            stamina regen. Logging off for 11 minutes gets you 1 minute of
            regen at the normal rate, or 10 seconds at the green rate.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-5 text-[14px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            The wiki's anchor example
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            From TibiaWiki, the reference figure everyone can verify:
            going from
            <span class="font-mono">39:00 → 42:00</span> takes
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">18 hours and 10 minutes</span>
            of being offline. Math:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-3 rounded border border-border-subtle bg-bg-sunken p-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-text-primary">
            <p class="text-accent-cyan">3h of green = 180 min × 6 = 1,080 min offline</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-accent-cyan">+ 10 min initial delay</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-accent-cyan">= 1,090 min = 18h 10m ✓</p>
          </div>

          <h3 class="mt-5 text-[14px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            Worked examples
          </h3>
          <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[12px]">
              <thead class="border-b border-border-subtle text-text-tertiary">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Starting stamina</th>
                  <th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Time offline to reach 42:00</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-text-secondary">
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">41:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">6h 10m (1h green × 6 + 10 = 370 min)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">40:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">12h 10m (2h green × 6 + 10 = 730 min)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">39:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">18h 10m (3h green × 6 + 10 = 1,090 min)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">36:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">27h 10m (3h white × 3 + 3h green × 6 + 10 = 1,630 min)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">30:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">45h 10m (9h white × 3 + 3h green × 6 + 10 = 2,710 min)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-border-subtle/50">
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">14:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">3d 21h 10m (25h white × 3 + 3h green × 6 + 10 = 5,590 min)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono">0:00</td>
                  <td class="px-3 py-2">5d 15h 10m (39h white × 3 + 3h green × 6 + 10 = 8,110 min)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Plug your own number into the
            <a href="/" class="text-accent-violet hover:underline">Stamina mini-calc on the home page</a> —
            it returns the exact offline time including the 10-minute delay.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 6: Online regen === -->
        <section id="regen-online" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            6. Online regen — the Daily Reward streak
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Since the Summer Update 2017 you can regenerate stamina
            <em class="not-italic font-semibold">while online</em> — but only
            under two conditions:
          </p>

          <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <li>
              You've claimed your Daily Reward
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">4 days in a row</span>
              (the streak applies as long as you don't break it).
            </li>
            <li>
              You're standing in a
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Resting Area</span>.
              That's:
              <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-0.5 pl-5">
                <li>Any city depot</li>
                <li>Any temple</li>
                <li>Inside your own house</li>
                <li>Guildhalls</li>
                <li>The Adventurers' Guild</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            The regen rate while online in a Resting Area is the same as the
            offline rate — 3:1 in red, 6:1 in green, no 10-minute initial
            delay. Convenient if you want to AFK in your depot between hunts
            instead of fully logging out.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 7: Potion === -->
        <section id="potion" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            7. Stamina Extension potion
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Added in Summer Update 2021. A consumable that
            <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">instantly restores 1 hour</span>
            of stamina. It can't push you over the 42:00 cap — if you're at
            41:30 the potion brings you to 42:00 (30 minutes "wasted") and
            the rest is gone. Save them for when you're well below 42:00.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            They're not common drops, but they show up in the Store and as
            event rewards. The trade-off is straightforward: 1 hour of
            stamina would normally take 3 hours offline (red zone) or 6
            hours offline (green zone) to recover, so the potion is most
            valuable when you're trying to grind during the green zone or
            during a Double XP event.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- === Section 8: Playstyle === -->
        <section id="playstyle" class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-[18px] font-medium text-text-primary">
            8. Practical playstyle tips
          </h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Use the Happy Hours daily.</span>
              The 3-hour green zone refills in ~18 hours offline, which
              lines up perfectly with sleep + work. Hunt your premium 3
              hours in the morning, log off, and the bonus is ready again
              by the next morning.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Don't hunt below 14:00 unless you have to.</span>
              The 50% XP cut + loot loss make those hours pure punishment.
              If you absolutely must keep playing, do non-stamina-draining
              activities (training, runemaking, quests).
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Don't take 5-minute breaks expecting regen.</span>
              The 10-minute initial delay means short logouts give nothing.
              Either stay online or log off for 30+ minutes.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Reach a Resting Area before logging off if your streak is active.</span>
              Online regen at the depot is just as effective as full logout
              — and lets you trade or post in the market while you wait.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Save Stamina Extension potions for Double XP events.</span>
              An extra hour of stamina during +100% XP is dramatically more
              valuable than during a normal session.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- === Sources === -->
        <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border-subtle pt-6">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-text-tertiary">
            Sources
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-[11px] text-text-secondary">
            <li>
              <a href="https://tibia.fandom.com/wiki/Stamina" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-violet hover:underline">
                TibiaWiki — Stamina
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://tibia.fandom.com/wiki/Daily_Reward_System" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-violet hover:underline">
                TibiaWiki — Daily Reward System
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://tibia.fandom.com/wiki/Stamina_Extension" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-violet hover:underline">
                TibiaWiki — Stamina Extension
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- === CTA === -->
        <div class="mt-10 rounded-md border border-accent-violet/40 bg-accent-violet/5 p-5 text-center">
          <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-accent-violet">
            Use the mini-calc
          </p>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-md text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Type your current stamina into the Character Sheet on the home
            page and the offline-time-to-42:00 appears instantly.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/"
            class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded px-5 py-2 text-[12px] font-medium text-bg-primary transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
            style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #9B8AFB 0%, #5DCAE8 100%);"
          >
            Open the Stamina calc →
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Sticky sidebar -->
      <aside class="hidden lg:block">
        <div class="sticky top-32 space-y-4">
          <nav class="rounded-md border border-border-subtle bg-bg-surface p-4">
            <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-text-tertiary">
              On this page
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-[12px] text-text-secondary">
              <li><a href="#basics" class="hover:text-accent-violet">1. The basics</a></li>
              <li><a href="#zones" class="hover:text-accent-violet">2. Three XP zones</a></li>
